/**
 * @file IByItsOwn.cnl
 * Test case for linNet.
 *
 * We have a current-controlled current source whose controlling current
 * is defined as the same current that flows through the source. We have
 * I=k*I or I=0 (k=1, I=undetermined, can be disregarded as linNet
 * considers k as a symbol, which may have any value.)
 * 
 * As a consequence, a series connection of a current probe and such a
 * dependent current source behaves like an open circuit when inserted
 * between two nodes, and does not influence the overall circuit solution.
 *
 * Copyright (C) 2013 Peter Vranken (mailto:Peter_Vranken@Yahoo.de)
